# Every later model track (v2_3_state, v4_0-v4_7, episode/wave/susceptibility/
# annual-FOI analyses) follows the same convention: compiled Stan models and
# stanfit bundles are large (often 20MB-700MB, some >1GB) and fully
# regenerable from the corresponding fit scripts, so ignore ALL .rds
# anywhere under 02_Script/ and 03_Output/ by default rather than listing
# every model version individually going forward. This does not affect the
# small foundational data caches already tracked under 01_Data/ or
# 02_Script/stan/ceara_weekly*.rds.
CHIK_CLIM/02_Script/**/*.rds
CHIK_CLIM/03_Output/**/*.rds

# Raw per-chain CmdStan-style sampler progress CSVs (used only for
# real-time HMC monitoring while a fit runs; can total several GB) and the
# legacy top-level progress-CSV cache -- regenerate by rerunning the fit.
CHIK_CLIM/02_Script/**/chains*/
CHIK_CLIM/02_Script/stan/sampling_progress/

# Raster / model outputs (large)
CHIK_CLIM/01_Data/*.tif
CHIK_CLIM/01_Data/*.zip

# Month panel is a regeneratable byproduct of 02_clean_chik_sinan_brazil.R
# (19MB CSV) -- keep ignored like the week panel above.
CHIK_CLIM/01_Data/chik_brazil_muni_month_*.csv
CHIK_CLIM/01_Data/chik_brazil_muni_month_*.rds

# Accidental Windows Explorer copy-paste duplicates
CHIK_CLIM/03_Output/**/* - 복사본.*

